1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,270
Hello everyone, this is Ria!

2
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:08,500
What shall we talk about today?

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,080
Today, it's animals! I'll talk about animals.

4
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:21,380
What kind of animal do you like the most?

5
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:28,800
I like cats! Cats are my favorite.

6
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:34,780
But I used to be scared of animals.

7
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:41,410
I was scared of cats and dogs.

8
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:51,070
Cats and dogs are animals that people commonly keep at home.

9
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:54,400
Commonly kept animals.

10
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:58,570
But I was scared of them.

11
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:00,540
I was scared.

12
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:02,140
Isn't that interesting?

13
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:11,340
When I was little, if I saw a cat or a dog, I would scream.

14
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:14,910
I screamed like this.

15
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:18,430
And I ran away.

16
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:21,070
I wanted to run away.

17
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:26,710
Let me tell you a really funny story.

18
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:33,720
When I was little, I was going home after school.

19
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:36,120
I was going home.

20
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:42,860
But there were two cats in front of my house.

21
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:49,420
There were two cats right in front of my house.

22
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:56,420
I was so surprised when I saw those cats.

23
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:59,620
My body froze.

24
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,220
It froze.

25
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:06,190
So I couldn't go into the house.

26
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:11,200
Thinking about it now, it's so funny.

27
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:17,380
I waited until my mom and dad came.

28
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:23,840
At that time, my parents were both working.

29
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,570
Both working.

30
00:02:25,570 --> 00:02:34,580
Both working means that both mom and dad have jobs.

31
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:43,300
When both mom and dad work, it's called "both working."

32
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,540
Both working.

33
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:56,850
Anyway, at that time, I was so scared of cats that I waited until my mom and dad came.

34
00:02:56,850 --> 00:03:00,480
I really wanted to cry then.

35
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:09,340
I wanted to go inside the house, but because of the cats, I couldn't go in and it was hard.

36
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:14,410
So I thought about it.

37
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:18,700
Why am I so scared of animals?

38
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:21,090
Am I scared of bugs?

39
00:03:21,090 --> 00:03:27,740
But I think there are a few reasons.

40
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:35,300
The first reason is that my mom is just like me.

41
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:41,240
My mom is still scared of animals.

42
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:46,600
Now I really like cats.

43
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:53,020
But my mom is still very scared.

44
00:03:53,020 --> 00:04:01,500
So I thought, "Did I inherit this from my mom?"

45
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:05,220
My older sister is the same.

46
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:11,680
A while ago, my sister and I went to Vietnam together.

47
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:21,220
But at the restaurant, cats kept coming to our table.

48
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:28,530
They kept coming to our table smelling the food.

49
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:31,200
I was okay with it.

50
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:35,760
But my sister kept screaming.

51
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:39,260
"What do we do!!! What do we do!!" she said.

52
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:48,930
But the interesting thing is that my dad really likes animals. He loves them.

53
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:58,420
My dad used to raise chickens, chicks, and dogs.

54
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:03,420
The second reason seems to be because of the environment.

55
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,710
Environment.

56
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:09,470
I grew up in the city.

57
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:18,270
The city I live in has a lot of apartments and buildings.

58
00:05:18,270 --> 00:05:24,300
There isn't much nature in Korean cities.

59
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,620
Nature.

60
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:32,920
So there aren't many chances to be close to animals.

61
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:43,790
Especially in Korea, children are not taught to get close to animals and nature when they are young.

62
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:46,460
They don't learn to get close.

63
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:55,490
So some people feel a little scared when they see animals.

64
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:57,360
Like me.

65
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:03,810
If a cat comes close, I get startled and avoid it.

66
00:06:03,810 --> 00:06:05,410
I avoid it.

67
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:17,090
But these days, kindergartens and schools in Korea seem to teach a little about this.

68
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:21,060
They teach a little at least.

69
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:26,780
You know, I went to Australia a while ago.

70
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,350
Australia.

71
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:33,060
I went to a region with a lot of sea.

72
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:41,340
I was resting on a beach towel in front of the sea.

73
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:50,410
But every time I went to the sea, there were a lot of dogs.

74
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:59,640
Dogs are a bit small, and "gae" (dog) is a bigger dog.

75
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:05,860
But there were a lot of dogs at the beach.

76
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,600
I was really surprised.

77
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:15,390
The culture of walking dogs by the sea was also interesting.

78
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:22,110
In Korea, it's not easy to see big dogs.

79
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:29,060
These things are very different between Australia and Korea.

80
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:37,910
How close animals and nature are, these things are very different.

81
00:07:37,910 --> 00:07:45,470
Everyone! In Korean, there is a word "gilgoyang-i."

82
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:47,460
Gilgoyang-i.

83
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:55,110
Gilgoyang-i means a cat that does not live in a person's house.

84
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:56,370
Gil.

85
00:07:56,370 --> 00:08:00,000
It means cats that live on the street.

86
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,260
So they are called street cats.

87
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:08,990
Are there many street cats in your country?

88
00:08:08,990 --> 00:08:14,290
There are a lot of street cats in Korea.

89
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:26,910
But instead of the word "street cat," in the past, Koreans called them "dodukgoyang-i."

90
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:28,290
Doduk!

91
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:34,590
Calling cats thieves... that's too harsh.

92
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:38,050
That's too harsh... right?

93
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:39,070
Doduk.

94
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:45,500
In Korean, "doduk" means a person who steals things.

95
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:53,760
Now you understand how unfriendly Koreans were to cats, right?

96
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:59,300
But now the world has changed a lot.

97
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:05,380
Now many people like cats.

98
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:14,450
So instead of calling them thief cats, they are now called street cats.

99
00:09:14,450 --> 00:09:20,900
Not bad thieves, just cats living on the street.

100
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:25,520
So they are called street cats.

101
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:37,570
These days in Korea, there seem to be quite a few people who feed and take care of these street cats.

102
00:09:37,570 --> 00:09:42,530
It's definitely different from the past.

103
00:09:42,530 --> 00:09:49,700
And do you know how Koreans call cats?

104
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:52,930
They have kind of nicknames.

105
00:09:52,930 --> 00:09:56,650
Nicknames for calling cats.

106
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:00,120
They call them very cutely.

107
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:05,240
How do cats meow, everyone?

108
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,720
What sound do they make?

109
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:12,530
What sound do cats make when they meow?

110
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:18,780
In Korean, it's not "Meow," but "Ya-ong."

111
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:22,210
Ya-ong Ya-ong Ya-ong.... (hahaha)

112
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:27,720
Did I sound a bit like a cat just now?

113
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:30,160
Cat impression.

114
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:35,490
A human doing a cat impression.

115
00:10:35,490 --> 00:10:39,200
Yes, in Korean it's "Ya-ong."

116
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:45,020
So "Ya-ong" is a nickname.

117
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:48,030
Or... "Nyang!"

118
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:50,030
(hahaha ㅠㅠ)

119
00:10:50,030 --> 00:10:56,570
"Nyang!" This is the sound cats make, "Nyang."

120
00:10:56,570 --> 00:11:01,670
So "Nyang" is also a nickname.

121
00:11:01,670 --> 00:11:07,160
It's my favorite nickname. Nyang-i!

122
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:13,890
Now, let's talk about the most important story.

123
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:21,060
I'll tell you why I like cats now.

124
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:23,070
I'll tell you.

125
00:11:23,070 --> 00:11:29,820
I used to be scared, but why do I like them now?

126
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:35,090
I mentioned Australia earlier.

127
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:40,600
I went to Australia a few years ago.

128
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,790
Australia.

129
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:48,390
There was a place I stayed at in Australia.

130
00:11:48,390 --> 00:11:49,750
Accommodation.

131
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:55,500
There was a cat at that accommodation.

132
00:11:55,500 --> 00:12:03,910
Before entering that place, I didn't know there was a cat.

133
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:12,100
But the owner suddenly told me there was a cat.

134
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:17,490
There was a cat in that house.

135
00:12:17,490 --> 00:12:21,500
I was so shocked then.

136
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,520
What should I do?

137
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:32,740
I worried, thinking, "I have to be in the same house with a cat?"

138
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:34,630
I was worried.

139
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:43,420
And finally, I met the cat in that house for the first time.

140
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,560
First meeting.

141
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,460
First meeting.

142
00:12:47,460 --> 00:12:50,400
This is the cat.

143
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:51,890
This cat.

144
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:53,880
It's a cheese cat.

145
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:58,110
In English, it's called a ginger cat.

146
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:04,110
In Korean, it's called a cheese cat.

147
00:13:04,110 --> 00:13:10,940
Because its color looks like cheese, it's called a cheese cat.

148
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,780
So cute, right?

149
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:20,000
But I saw the cat from very far away.

150
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,040
I was scared, so I avoided it a bit.

151
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:37,010
I really don’t understand why people are so afraid of animals... Looking back now, I just can’t get it.

152
00:13:37,010 --> 00:13:39,530
I really don’t get it.

153
00:13:39,530 --> 00:13:46,370
Then one day, the owner left the house.

154
00:13:46,370 --> 00:13:50,270
Went out.

155
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:56,690
It was just me and the cat left alone at home.

156
00:13:56,690 --> 00:13:58,310
Just the two of us.

157
00:13:58,310 --> 00:14:01,760
Doesn’t it sound like a movie?

158
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:05,620
Movie title: "The Cat and Me"

159
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:08,050
"The Cat and Me"

160
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:16,040
Anyway, the cat kept coming into my room.

161
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:19,970
It kept coming into my room.

162
00:14:19,970 --> 00:14:28,160
But as I kept spending time with the cat like this, I grew attached.

163
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,180
Grew attached.

164
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:32,290
I got attached.

165
00:14:32,290 --> 00:14:38,740
One day, the cat came onto my bed.

166
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:42,260
It slept on my bed.

167
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:44,220
We slept together.

168
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:48,740
I even covered it with a blanket.

169
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:54,200
This kind of experience is really fun.

170
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:59,360
I used to be really scared of cats.

171
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:04,750
Remember how I couldn’t even enter the house?

172
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:10,220
But gradually, I became friends with the cat.

173
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,780
Gradually.

174
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:17,940
I even started to touch the cat.

175
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:20,600
I started touching it.

176
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:26,910
Sometimes, the cat licked me.

177
00:15:26,910 --> 00:15:28,870
It licked me.

178
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:32,860
This word is a bit hard to pronounce, right everyone?

179
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:36,900
It licked me.

180
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:48,330
Wow, I touched the cat and the cat licked me... This is a miracle. A miracle!

181
00:15:48,330 --> 00:15:56,780
One day, I was coming back home after going out.

182
00:15:56,780 --> 00:16:03,230
But the cat was waiting for me.

183
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:11,900
The cat was at the door, saw me, and came up to me.

184
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:13,920
It came up to me.

185
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:17,040
It was so amazing.

186
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:24,320
Everyone, originally... what kind of personality do cats have?

187
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:27,120
I mentioned this before.

188
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:31,730
Cats are independent animals.

189
00:16:31,730 --> 00:16:34,270
Independent animals.

190
00:16:34,270 --> 00:16:38,480
Cats like to be alone.

191
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:45,510
But this cat acted unusually like a dog.

192
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:54,840
A cat that acts like a dog is called "gaenyang" in Korean.

193
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,310
Gaenyang.

194
00:16:56,310 --> 00:16:59,870
"Nyang" — I mentioned this earlier, right?

195
00:16:59,870 --> 00:17:03,730
It’s a nickname for cats.

196
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:08,550
Put together, it’s called "gaenyang."

197
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:18,980
A cat that is affectionate like a dog and follows its owner well is called "gaenyang."

198
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:24,050
A cat that follows its owner well.

199
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:33,450
Anyway, the cheese cat at the Australian house was really a gaenyang.

200
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:40,350
So I called this cat "Cheese Nyang."

201
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:45,270
It actually had an English name.

202
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:58,110
The owner had a separate English name for it, but I just called it by the Korean name.

203
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,190
Cheese Nyang.

204
00:18:00,190 --> 00:18:06,240
This cat really loved people.

205
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:11,720
It was a cat that really liked people.

206
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:17,980
So I got very attached.

207
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:21,080
I got very attached.

208
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:30,670
When I parted with this cat at the end, I looked at it and said in my heart,

209
00:18:30,670 --> 00:18:35,930
Will I ever see you again?

210
00:18:35,930 --> 00:18:39,230
Can we meet again?

211
00:18:39,230 --> 00:18:40,770
(lol...)

212
00:18:40,770 --> 00:18:44,160
This is not a love story, everyone!

213
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:51,320
Meeting you in such a faraway country was fate.

214
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,020
It was fate.

215
00:18:53,020 --> 00:19:00,740
Be healthy! Take care! I said this and came back to Korea.

216
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:08,670
I think people who have pets will understand this feeling.

217
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:11,030
I think they will understand.

218
00:19:11,030 --> 00:19:18,100
Of course, this cat was not my pet.

219
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:30,590
I wasn’t the owner, but still, during the short time we spent together, I got very attached.

220
00:19:30,590 --> 00:19:35,520
I still miss it so much.

221
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:46,460
Everyone, did you listen well to my cat history so far?

222
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:55,150
This wasn’t just a simple podcast about how cute cats are.

223
00:19:55,150 --> 00:20:00,410
It was about my somewhat weak side?

224
00:20:00,410 --> 00:20:03,710
My weak side when I was young?

225
00:20:03,710 --> 00:20:09,020
How I was scared of cats and animals?

226
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:18,330
And the story of the Australian Cheese Nyang that I still miss so much.

227
00:20:18,330 --> 00:20:26,940
That’s why I especially like cheese cats even now.

228
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:30,940
There are many kinds of cats.

229
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,840
Among them, cheese cats!

230
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:40,780
Among them, I like cheese cats the most.

231
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:48,350
Sometimes, students I teach send me pictures of their cats.

232
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:53,550
They send pictures of the cats they raise.

233
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:57,790
Every time I see them, it’s so healing.

234
00:20:57,790 --> 00:21:01,630
I really scream out loud.

235
00:21:01,630 --> 00:21:07,790
So cute! I really love you!!! (lol) I scream like that.

236
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:16,510
Before, I screamed because I was scared, but now I scream because I like them.

237
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:18,560
It’s the opposite now.

238
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:22,930
I scream because they’re so cute.

239
00:21:22,930 --> 00:21:26,080
“Ah, so cute.” Like that.

240
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:36,150
So if you ever have a cat, please tell me a lot about your cat.

241
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:40,220
Please brag about your cat to me.

242
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:41,410
Brag.

243
00:21:41,410 --> 00:21:49,890
It’s okay to tell me the name, or write about its personality in Korean.

244
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:54,370
Whether it’s a gaenyang or not, things like that.

245
00:21:54,370 --> 00:21:58,770
Sometimes I think about this.

246
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:05,310
I wish we could upload pictures in the YouTube comments.

247
00:22:05,310 --> 00:22:12,000
It would be nice if both I and you could upload pictures.

248
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,450
Wouldn’t that be fun?

249
00:22:14,450 --> 00:22:20,450
It would be fun if we could upload pictures in the comments.

250
00:22:20,450 --> 00:22:25,630
But unfortunately, we can’t upload pictures.

251
00:22:25,630 --> 00:22:32,290
So, in your country, what kind of image do cats have?

252
00:22:32,290 --> 00:22:38,130
Just street cats? Or more like sneaky cats?

253
00:22:38,130 --> 00:22:42,910
And do you like cats?

254
00:22:42,910 --> 00:22:49,520
I think most countries probably like cats.

255
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:54,210
Please tell me a lot about cats.

256
00:22:54,210 --> 00:22:55,480
Okay?

257
00:22:55,480 --> 00:23:01,490
Then let’s meet next time with a more fun story.

258
00:23:01,490 --> 00:23:07,710
